## 2. Installing OpenCode

OpenCode runs on macOS, Linux, and Windows (via WSL 2).

### Install Script

```bash
curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/install | bash
```

After installation, restart your terminal or run:

```bash
source ~/.bashrc   # or ~/.zshrc if you use zsh
```

### Verify It Works

```bash
opencode --version
```

You should see something like `2.3.0`.

### First Launch

```bash
opencode
```

This opens the TUI (Terminal User Interface). You'll see a chat window.
Type `/help` to see available commands.

> **Don't worry if nothing happens yet** — you need to configure a model first.
> We'll do that next.

