## 6. The TUI: Your Main Workspace

When you run `opencode`, you enter the **TUI** (Terminal User Interface).
This is where you'll spend 90% of your time.

### Key Controls

| Key | Action |
|---|---|
| Type a message | Chat with the agent |
| `Ctrl+P` | Open settings / command palette |
| `Ctrl+T` | Cycle through model variants |
| `Ctrl+C` | Cancel the current response |
| `/help` | List all commands |

### Your First Session

1. Run `opencode` from your project folder
2. Type: *"List all the files in this project"*
3. Watch the agent use `shell` to run `ls` and report back
4. Then ask: *"What does the README say?"*
5. Watch it use `read` to open the file

**What you're seeing:** The agent is not just generating text — it's actually
running commands on your computer.

### The Sidebar

On the right side of the TUI you'll see:

```
Context
147,529 tokens
37% used
$5.56 spent
```

This shows:
- **Tokens**: How much text the model is processing
- **% used**: How much of the context window is full
- **Spent**: Estimated cost of this session so far

