## 12. Mobile and Remote

### Coding From Your Phone

One of the best parts of AI coding: you can keep working from anywhere.

```bash
opencode pair --remote
```

This creates an **OpenTunnel** connection. Scan the QR code with your phone
and you're connected.

```
┌──────────────┐         ┌──────────────────┐
│ Your computer │ ◄────► │ Your phone        │
│ (agent runs)  │ Tunnel │ (chat interface)  │
└──────────────┘         └──────────────────┘
```

### Remote Server

You can also run OpenCode on a different machine entirely:

```bash
# On the remote machine:
OPENCODE_PASSWORD="your-password" opencode serve --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096

# On your local machine:
OPENCODE_PASSWORD="your-password" opencode --server http://<hostname>:4096
```

This is useful for:
- A powerful cloud VM
- A Raspberry Pi at home
- A beefy desktop you SSH into

### Practical Example: Full Mobile Workflow

1. Start a session on your computer: *"What's the meaning of life?"*
2. Open the same session on your phone
3. Ask a follow-up: *"When did it change from 42 to 6-7?"*
4. Notice both terminals stay in sync

