## Quick Reference

### Essential Commands

```bash
opencode                    # Open the TUI
opencode run "prompt"       # One-shot prompt
opencode pair               # Generate Web UI link
opencode pair --remote      # Generate remote (mobile) link
opencode models             # List available models
opencode service status     # Check if server is running
opencode service restart    # Restart the background server
```

### Config File Structure

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "provider/model-id",
  "permissions": [
    { "action": "tool", "resource": "pattern", "effect": "allow|ask|deny" },
  ],
  "providers": {
    "provider-name": {
      "settings": { "apiKey": "{env:VARIABLE}" },
      "models": { "model-id": { "name": "Human Name" } },
    },
  },
}
```

### Key Concepts

| Concept | Summary |
|---|---|
| **Agent harness** | OpenCode itself — it runs the tools |
| **LLM / Model** | The "brain" that decides what to do |
| **Provider** | Who serves the model to you |
| **Tool** | A function the agent can call |
| **Skill** | Reusable instructions (a playbook for a task) |
| **Agent** | A named configuration/persona for the assistant |
| **Context** | Everything the model can see (history, files, instructions) |
| **Plugin** | Adds custom tools and features |
| **Permission** | Controls which tools run automatically |
| **Token** | Unit of text the model processes |
| **Variant** | A model configuration (e.g., reasoning level) |
| **Sandbox** | Isolated environment for safety |

